title: Repos
pid: f16e9c7d-6271-4136-87e4-a9332743ba45
body: |2-
    - Request: ((request . "repos"))
    - Response: LP =((response-type repos) (restriction "NAME")
      (foreign-repos "shown") (repos ((name "NAME") (path "PATH")
      (abbreviation "ABBR") (owned "true") (shown "true")) ...))=, one
      entry per configured skgrepo, in fold order: declaration order, the
      owned ones in privacy order (most public first; see "skgconfig.toml
      > Skgrepos"). =PATH= is the skgrepo's path as the config writes it:
      relative to the data root when it lies below it, else absolute.
      =(abbreviation ...)= appears only when the skgrepo has one,
      configured or derived (the =abbreviation= field of "Skgrepos").
      =owned= is "false" for a skgrepo whose entry says
      =foreign = true=. =shown= is whether the connection's skgrepo
      restriction shows the skgrepo. =(restriction ...)= and
      =(foreign-repos ...)= are that restriction, as "skgrepo
      restriction" reports it.
    - The endpoint is read-only and lists every skgrepo of the config,
      restricted or not; =shown= says which the restriction keeps out.
    - Logic: =server/serve/handlers/repos.rs=.
